title: delete_ref has no compare-and-swap, so every guarded delete has a race window
updated: 2026-08-10T01:40:24Z
---

Found while fixing #56.

App::karr::Git::delete_ref goes through libgit2 git_reference_remove(repo, name),
which takes no expected-old OID. So a delete cannot be guarded: whatever karr
checked before calling it may have changed by the time it runs.

That matters for the claim guards added in #56. Deleting a task re-checks the
claim immediately before the delete, which closes the minutes-long window behind
the confirmation prompt, but leaves a microsecond one. Same shape as #44/#46
before the CAS work, just much smaller.

The guarded form already exists upstream: Git::Native::Reference->delete
operates on a looked-up reference, and libgit2 refuses it when the ref no longer
matches what was looked up. It is simply not wired into App::karr::Git, which
only exposes the name-based removal.

Work: add a CAS delete alongside write_ref_cas -- read_ref_with_oid, then delete
via the looked-up reference, reporting the same retryable outcome
(is_not_matched / GIT_ELOCKED) that retry_contended already understands. Then
move the guarded delete paths onto it.

Note #51 (delete_ref discards its error and increments WRITES regardless) is the
same function; whoever takes either should take both.
Fixed and merged into main (fa79722); full suite green at 93 files / 630 tests.
Reproduced before the fix, regression test verified to fail against the pre-fix
code. #94 additionally confirmed empirically that libgit2 lookup-based delete
really does guard: moving the ref underneath it answers "old reference value
does not match".
